# Arm B retrain results watcher. The project log 10b.
#
# THE `cd` IS LOAD BEARING. Cron starts in $HOME, so a relative ./grid/...
# would resolve against the wrong root. That is the same relative-path failure
# as the project log 4c, 5h and 10, and it has now been made four times in this
# project, twice while writing this very line.
#
# Install with:  crontab grid/arms/armb_watcher.cron
# Remove with:   crontab -r
#
# A failed cycle deliberately leaves grid_results_arms/.last_pull untouched, so
# the file's age is the age of the last REAL pull rather than the last attempt.
# If .last_pull is older than two hours while the chain is running, the watcher
# is dead and must be restarted.
*/30 * * * * cd . && ./grid/fetch_results.sh --arms >> grid_results_arms_watch.log 2>&1
